    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d495">

                <pb facs="0554" n="1232" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1232"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Corwin</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 61.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-11-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 26, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of October 27 (No. 34) has
                    been received. It presents, in a very brief, yet a very comprehensive way, the
                    political and military situation of Mexico.</p>
                <p>Under date of the 24th instant I addressed you a despatch, (No. 61,) which was
                    forwarded by the mail of yesterday, and for which you will please to consider
                    the present a substitute, the first of this number having been cancelled.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thomas Corwin</hi>, Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
